# How to cite Open Chiari. GitHub shows this as "Cite this repository"; Zenodo reads .zenodo.json.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Open Chiari 3D model or figures, please cite them as below and give the credit in LICENSE-MODEL.md."
title: "Open Chiari: an open 3D anatomy model of Chiari malformation type I"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Borgfeld
    given-names: Matthew
    affiliation: Open Chiari
url: "https://openchiari.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ARCFrontierSystems/OpenChiari"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - Chiari malformation
  - Chiari I
  - syringomyelia
  - 3D anatomy
  - patient education
  - open educational resource
abstract: >-
  Open 3D models and figures of the head and upper neck at the midline, in four conditions: typical anatomy,
  Chiari malformation type I, Chiari I with a syrinx, and after decompression surgery. Built for patient education.
  Every shape and measurement is traced to a source in docs/EVIDENCE.md and checked automatically
  (npm run model:check). Illustrations, not medical images. The model is CC BY-SA 4.0 (LICENSE-MODEL.md),
  adapted from Z-Anatomy (CC BY-SA 4.0) and BodyParts3D, © The Database Center for Life Science (CC BY-SA 2.1 JP);
  the website code is MIT (LICENSE).
